title: Consolidation of the Christian Right
subtitle: The <span style="color: #000000;">**Center**</span> mergers with the <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span>
view-if: year >= 1931 and z_in_government and dnvp_in_government and cvp_merger_countdown < 0
max-visits: 1
tags: event
priority: 3
new-page: true

= Consolidation of the Christian Right

With the election of both Adam Stegerwald as chairman of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> and Gottfried Treviranus to the <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span>, the two greatest proponents of uniting the two christian parties, a party merger has always been a possibility, that has now turned into reality

- @congress: The newly formed <span style="color: #000000;">**Christian People's Party**</span> will now hold its first congress to determine their leader.

@congress
on-arrival:{!
    Q.cvp_balance = 0;

    Q.cvp_balance = Q.cvp_balance + (pro_republic - 50.)/20.;
    Q.cvp_balance = Q.cvp_balance - (nationalism - 50.)/20.;

    Q.cvp_balance += (Q.z_votes - Q.bvp_votes)/10.;
    Q.cvp_balance -= Q.dnvp_votes/10.;

    if (spd_right > spd_left) Q.cvp_balance += 1;
!}
go-to: dietrich

@dietrich
subtitle: Dietrich was the former leader of the <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s business wing.
on-arrival: dvp_leader = "Dietrich"; democratic_strength += 10; democratization += 1; democratic_dissent -= 5
face-image: img/portraits/DietrichHermann.jpg
go-to: nfvp_formed

Supported by the party’s newly integrated Democrats and Progressives, along with a portion of our own liberals, Hermann Dietrich is set to lead our party towards a more generally liberal direction, holding little emphasis on nationalism and instead pursuing a more cooperative approach to democracy. Naturally, the party’s remaining Nationalists have already collectively agreed to abandon the party, with the Industrialists harbouring heavy skepticism in their role within the new NFVP.


